; expect 42
; A string literal pattern TESTS its text instead of binding like a
; variable and swallowing every scrutinee. Both scrutinees here are
; literals; 996-match-string-content.ax is the case where one is
; built at run time, which is where comparing the interned header's
; ADDRESS (the rule until 2026-08-21) answered 0 for equal text.
(:: f (-> String Int))
(fn (f s) (match s ("hi" 40) (x 2)))
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (+ (f "hi") (f "yo")))
